# All the stuff with that async job

- set_trial_session_lambda (sqs job):
  - Fed into by an sqs, takes trial session id, and a single docket id
  - Called by setNoticesForCalendaredTrialSessionInteractor with path
    /async/trial-sessions/:trialSessionId/generate-notices
  - setNoticesForCalendaredTrialSessionInteractor (orchestrator) will send messages for each docket ID in a trial session and wait for them all to finish.
    - Creates trial-session-processing-job-${trialSessionId} to track progress of entire job
    - Creates set-notices-for-trial-session-job-${jobId} to track progress of each case
    - Sends SQS message to invoke set_trial_session_lambda for each case
    - Each set_trial_session_lambda will add a new attribute on set-notices-for-trial-session-job-${jobId} and decrementing the unfinished counter
    - Checks unfinished counter to see if all the processes have finished.
    - Marks trial-session-processing-job-${trialSessionId} done

The whole process is just using dynamo to track the progress of this job. We can translate this to use a table for the same purpose. If we want to keep functionality the same we can use a jsonb array to keep track of all the individual cases. We may want to merge both dynamo objects into a single table, I didn't see any reason why they need to be separate.
